id: pm-swarm-atomic-close
title: Resume fenced close with an SDK workspace transaction
description: "One commitWorkspaceTransaction owns ordered native metadata update and close steps, deterministic deriveMutationTransactionId identity and SDK compensation/resume. validateWorkspaceTransactionIdentity plus exact journal-bound native versions and complete document hashes prove ownership; free-text messages and mutable markers cannot authorize rollback. Native item-lock admission preserves peer edits."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: concurrency
created_at: "2026-10-26T21:32:19.770Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T04:14:24.784Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: One SDK workspace transaction containing update then close; deterministic transaction identity; non-Git interruption at every forward boundary and fresh-process resume without duplicate history or lost fields; ordinary failure compensation and retry; no swarm_partial_commit path for close.; Resumed compensation verifies latest owned SDK history under the item lock and never deletes peer changes from a prior refused rollback
parent: pm-swarm-y972
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T22:01:31.001Z",codex-agent,"Native compound-close regression and partial-prefix peer-preservation test pass. Separate behavioral reversions of the committed-successor observer and partial-commit refusal each fail their regression once, exit 1; restored positives pass. This verifies guarded per-stage behavior and truthful receipts, not a single atomic close. The SDK gap remains open."
  "2026-10-26T23:21:05.145Z",codex-agent,"Implemented public commitItemMutations on commitWorkspaceTransaction, with deriveMutationTransactionId and an owned recovery receipt. Initial focused recovery suite passed 11/11: seven exact SDK forward boundaries resume in fresh CLI processes with exactly update then close and no duplicate history; ordinary failure compensates the metadata step, then retry completes once. This corrects the prior SDK-gap claim; no lifecycle or journal engine was reimplemented. Expanded peer and writer-inventory tests are running."
  "2026-10-26T23:25:52.970Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"SDK close journal resumes\" test/close-transaction.test.ts fails when only the prior unjournaled SharedTracker.close function is restored (exit 1, one failure). Disabling only the persisted-receipt resume condition fails eight results; removing only journaled-mode admission fails seven results by returning partial-commit errors instead of SDK interruptions. All three probes restored source byte-for-byte: sixteen expected failing results total. The restored 25-test suite passes, covering seven forward crashes, four compensation crashes, fresh-process resume, seven private-peer transitions and committed replay ownership checks."
  "2026-10-26T23:36:30.486Z",codex-agent,"Final recovery suite passes 26/26, including short-ID admission resumed by canonical ID. Transaction identity and cached-token lookup use the SDK-resolved canonical id; owned token cleanup remains inside the lease. Replacing only canonical resolution with the raw caller id makes the canonical-item regression fail once (exit 1), then exact source restoration passes. Four probes now produce 17 expected failures. Fencing remains 11/11; journaled close never reports swarm_partial_commit. Full isolated npm and Bun CI is next."
  "2026-10-26T23:51:56.539Z",codex-agent,"Current-head CI exposed two retained refusal regressions: the new path read SDK usage before rejecting stale state, and malformed stored fences lost their repair diagnostic. Restored pure inspectItem admission before the effectful host read, then re-evaluate the fresh snapshot before the transaction. Stored malformed fences retain the established repair message. Added service-capable bound-client fallback coverage and explicit resource isolation checks. Restored targeted close/refusal/review suite passes 33/33, including 27 close tests. Removing only pure preflight fails the prepared-state regression once; removing only malformed-generation validation fails the repair-diagnostic regression once. Both probes exit 1 and restore exact source. Six close-related probes total 19 expected failures."
  "2026-10-27T00:03:51.815Z",codex-agent,"CI at c98b763 passed all 413 tests on Node 26 and stopped only on an uncovered legacy baseline branch. Added a real native SDK-only claim without a swarm token: interruption, resume without a token, exactly update then close, generation one and byte-identical committed replay all pass. The focused 28-test close suite passes; focused coverage confirms the legacy branch is exercised, with remaining focused-only omissions covered by the retained malformed and empty-note tests. Changing only the legacy baseline from zero to one fails its regression once (exit 1); exact restoration passes. Seven probes now produce 20 expected failures. No production code, thresholds or exclusions changed in this follow-up."
  "2026-10-27T00:31:11.214Z",codex-agent,"Verified at e1286a3056eb8ac17d0551c052bb46e6c6cdae85: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40424027439 . npm on Node 22 and 26 and Bun on Node 26 each pass 414 suite tests plus four packed-acceptance results, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; coverage is 100/100/100/100 across 35 sources at unchanged thresholds, with at most two workers. The 28-test close suite proves seven forward interruptions, four compensation interruptions, fresh-process and canonical-ID recovery, native tokenless generation-one recovery, peer preservation and replay without duplicates. Seven behavioral revert probes produced 20 expected failures before exact restoration. Both mutation kinds are expressed by public commitItemMutations on commitWorkspaceTransaction; atomic close is not an SDK gap. Closing this item under the explicit orchestrator instruction."
  "2026-10-27T00:39:34.137Z",codex-agent,"Final retry audit reproduced a cross-attempt compensation bug on a real scratch tracker: after the first rollback was correctly refused on a public peer comment, a fresh retry adopted that peer state and SDK restore removed the comment. Reopening this explicitly scoped recovery item to fix the class before completion. Recovery receipts must be correlated with the latest SDK history entry before a new request adopts pending transaction state; a foreign latest writer must yield a typed conflict without touching item, history or journal. This is a package admission defect, not a missing SDK mutation kind."
  "2026-10-27T00:53:07.283Z",codex-agent,"Cross-attempt ownership correction passes the expanded 36-test close suite. Public SDK history reads correlate the latest actor, reserved bulk marker and native update/close/restore operation with the close receipt. Pure/fresh preflight and the native item-lock guard all check it. Four real peer variants (comment, title, body, copied marker on a comment) preserve item, history and journal bytes on retry; owned close-step compensation still resumes, and unreadable history yields a safe typed refusal. Four behavioral reversions fail as expected: remove foreign-receipt rejection (five failures), omit the final native-lock check (one), remove unreadable-history translation (one), reject owned restore receipts (one). Exact restoration follows each probe. Eleven close probes now produce 28 expected failures."
  "2026-10-27T01:01:21.246Z",codex-agent,"Final recovery acceptance is verified locally: 36/36 close tests, 10/10 installed SDK-copy tests, eight restored ownership-focused checks, typecheck, lint, documented declarations and zero duplication. The cross-attempt peer-loss reproduction now refuses without changing item/history/journal bytes; checks run under the native item lock. Eleven behavioral probes yield 28 expected failures before restoration. Closing under the explicit orchestrator instruction with these recovery proofs; final-head npm/Bun release gates are still required before the final report. Record final tracking state before CI to avoid a second unchanged-source full run; reopen if CI exposes a behavioral defect."
  "2026-10-27T03:02:04.550Z",codex-agent,"Reopened for auto round 2: free-text transaction markers are not ownership evidence. Replacing this inference with journal-anchored SDK transaction recovery and testing forged same-author update markers across retries without losing the peer mutation."
  "2026-10-27T04:04:06.302Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 2 revert proof: restored only the old completeClaim implementation and ran node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"copied same-author\" test/close-journal-ownership.test.ts. Exit 1, 0/4 pass, four genuine behavioral failures: retries incorrectly accept the copied messages and erase the peer updates. Restored the journal/version fix; ownership suite passes 5/5. Recovery no longer reads history message text for ownership."
